    "result_text": "Behavior preserved, probe removed. Done.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agreed with both findings and collapsed the duplicated logic into single homes:\n\n1. **One problem+json skeleton.** Extracted a single `shapeProblem(detail, e, url, fallbackDetail)` normalizer that applies `type`, `title`, the `timestamp`/`schemaValidationErrors` members, and a fallback `detail`\u2014each write idempotent so a more specific handler's values (bespoke message, populated `schemaValidationErrors`) are preserved. Both paths now render through it:\n   - `detailBuild(...)` is now a thin factory (`ProblemDetail.forStatus(status)` \u2192 `shapeProblem(...)`) used by the six custom `@ExceptionHandler` methods.\n   - `handleExceptionInternal(...)` calls the same `shapeProblem(...)` instead of re-implementing the five-member assembly inline.\n\n   The skeleton is now defined in exactly one place; adding or renaming a member means editing one method.\n\n2. **One `type`-URL derivation.** `detailBuild` now takes a resolved `String url`. The custom handlers pass `requestUrl(HttpServletRequest)` (returns `getRequestURL().toString()`), and the framework-hook variant `requestUrl(WebRequest)` unwraps the `ServletWebRequest` and **defers to the same `requestUrl(HttpServletRequest)`**, falling back to the request description only when it isn't a servlet request. The `StringBuffer` plumbing is gone.\n\nBoth findings were quality/structure only, so behavior is unchanged: the acceptance test passes, and I re-verified the framework path (malformed JSON) still returns `400 application/problem+json` with `type`/`title`/`status`/`detail`. Full suite is green.",
